    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective date: 3 October 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: 3 October 2026</p>

    <p>Maya is an AI companion application. This policy explains what information
       we collect, why we collect it, who we share it with, and the control you
       have over it. It applies to the Maya mobile application and to this
       website.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p><strong>The short version.</strong> We collect what is needed to run the
         app: your account details, the messages you send, and your usage of the
         service. Your messages are processed by Google's Gemini AI to generate
         replies. We do not sell your personal information, and you can delete
         your account and all associated data from inside the app at any time.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>

    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address and, if you
          provide one, your display name. If you sign in with Google, we receive
          your email address and basic profile information from Google. We never
          receive your Google password.</li>
      <li><strong>Conversation content.</strong> The messages you send to your
          companions, including any images you choose to attach.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice call audio.</strong> When you make a voice call, your
          microphone audio is streamed to Google's Gemini Live service so the
          companion can hear and respond to you in real time. Audio is processed
          to produce the reply and a text transcript; the transcript is stored
          with your conversation history.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile choices.</strong> The companions you talk to, the
          gifts you send, and your in-app preferences and theme settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information created as you use Maya</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Activity data.</strong> Message counts, conversation
          timestamps, daily check-in streaks, and your relationship progress
          with each companion.</li>
      <li><strong>Virtual currency records.</strong> Your balance of in-app
          "diamonds" and the transaction ledger that records how they were
          earned or spent. These records exist to keep balances accurate.</li>
      <li><strong>Memory facts.</strong> Short factual notes the service derives
          from your conversations (for example, that you have a sister, or that
          you dislike mornings) so that a companion can recall them later. You
          can review and clear these in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data.</strong> Device type, operating system version,
          app version, language, and your timezone (used to determine when your
          daily check-in becomes available).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
    <p>We do not collect your contacts, your precise location, your photos
       library, or any data from other apps on your device. We do not use
       third-party advertising trackers and we do not track you across other
       apps or websites.</p>

    <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and secure your account, and to sign you in.</li>
      <li>To generate companion replies — this is why your messages are sent to
          our AI provider (see section 4).</li>
      <li>To let a companion remember earlier conversations and respond in
          character.</li>
      <li>To keep your conversation history available across sessions and
          devices.</li>
      <li>To operate in-app features such as gifts, streaks and daily rewards.</li>
      <li>To detect abuse, prevent fraud, and keep the service safe.</li>
      <li>To diagnose crashes and improve reliability and performance.</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your conversations to train our own
       artificial-intelligence models, and we do not sell your personal
       information to anyone.</p>

    <h2>3. Legal bases for processing</h2>
    <p>Where required by law, we rely on the following legal bases:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Providing the app and its features</td><td>Performance of our contract with you</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Keeping the service safe and preventing abuse</td><td>Our legitimate interests</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sending service and security notices</td><td>Performance of our contract, or legal obligation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Optional communications about new features</td><td>Your consent, which you may withdraw at any time</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>

    <p>We share information only with service providers who help us run Maya,
       and only to the extent they need it:</p>

    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th><th>What they receive</th><th>Why</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google (Gemini API)</td>
        <td>Your message text, recent conversation context, and voice call audio</td>
        <td>To generate companion replies and synthesize the companion's voice</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Supabase</td>
        <td>Your account and all data described in section 1</td>
        <td>Database, authentication and file storage infrastructure</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google Sign-In</td>
        <td>Your email address and basic profile</td>
        <td>Only if you choose to sign in with Google</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <p>When your messages are sent to Google's Gemini API, Google's handling of
       that data is governed by
       <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Gemini API terms</a>
       and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, to enforce our Terms
       of Service, or to protect the rights and safety of our users or the
       public. If Maya is ever involved in a merger or acquisition, your
       information may transfer as part of that transaction; we will notify you
       before your information becomes subject to a different privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>We keep your information for as long as your account exists. When you
       delete your account, we delete your profile, conversations, memory facts,
       call transcripts, virtual currency records and stored media. Deletion is
       permanent and cannot be undone.</p>
    <p>Some records may be retained for a limited period where we are legally
       required to do so, such as financial records connected to purchases, or
       where needed to resolve an open dispute or security incident.</p>

    <h2>6. Your rights and choices</h2>
    <p>You can, from inside the app:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access and correct</strong> your profile information.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete individual conversations</strong> and clear stored
          memory facts.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete your entire account</strong> and all associated data.
          This is available in Settings, and the deletion is immediate.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign out</strong> of the app at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to request a copy
       of your data, to object to or restrict certain processing, or to lodge a
       complaint with your local data-protection authority. To make a request,
       email us at the address in section 10.</p>

    <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>Maya is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly
       collect personal information from them. If you are under 13, please do
       not use the app. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with
       personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
    <p>If you are between 13 and 18, please use Maya only with the involvement
       and permission of a parent or guardian.</p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>We protect your information with encryption in transit, row-level access
       controls that restrict every record to its owner, and a server-side
       design in which API credentials are never stored on your device. No
       system is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security —
       but we design so that a compromise of one account cannot expose
       another's data.</p>

    <h2>9. International transfers and changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>Our service providers operate globally, so your information may be
       processed in countries other than your own. Where required, we rely on
       appropriate safeguards for such transfers.</p>
    <p>We may update this policy as Maya evolves. When we make a material change
       we will notify you in the app before it takes effect, and we will update
       the date at the top of this page.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions, requests or concerns about privacy:</p>
    <p><a href="mailto:swapnilbiswas282@gmail.com">swapnilbiswas282@gmail.com</a></p>
